me Bayer matrix the covers are cut\n         with, so the object is made of the covers'' own material. The panel\n         stays frontal and the cover sits in its recess at 1x. -->\n    <div class=\"hero-obj\">\n      <div class=\"flex\">\n        <img class=\"flex-shell\" src=\"assets/flex-shell.png\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"584\" height=\"704\">\n        <!-- The whitepaper, because it is the newest title and the one the\n             shelf leads with. Swapping this line and its alt text is the whole\n             of changing which book the front page shows. -->\n        <!-- THE READER, RUNNING. Not a picture of one: this is `sim/`, the\n             same pagination and the same atlases the device carries, in the\n             recess the drawn Flex leaves for a screen. A visitor taps the\n             glass and the page turns, which is the only honest way to show\n             what the thing is. `?bare` strips the bench''s own frame so the\n             only device on the page is the one drawn around it. -->\n        <span class=\"plate-box flex-plate\">\n          <iframe class=\"plate live\" src=\"try/index.html?book=bitcoin&amp;bare\" title=\"The reader, running: tap the screen to turn a page\" loading=\"lazy\" scrolling=\"no\"></iframe>\n          <!-- The glass. A layer over the panel, not a change to it: the\n               reader''s pixels are the device''s pixels and nothing here is\n               allowed to alter one. It takes no clicks, so a tap goes\n               through to the page underneath. -->\n          <span class=\"glass\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n          <!-- The sheen: the one thing on the page that moves, and the only\n               reason a visitor learns the drawing is live without touching\n               it first. -->\n          <span class=\"sheen\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        </span>\n        <span class=\"tapme\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Tap to read</span>\n      </div>\n      <!-- The cue. A visitor has no reason to guess that a drawing is live, so\n           the page says it once, quietly, under the device rather than over\n           the book. -->\n      <p class=\"hero-cue\">Tap the screen. It is the reader, running.</p>\n    </div>\n\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ── the questions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->\n  <div class=\"shelf-head head-flush\" id=\"questions\">\n    <h2>Questions</h2>\n  </div>\n\n  <section class=\"faq\">\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>Why did you turn a hardware wallet into a reader?&nbsp;</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>\"Because there''s an e-ink screen there.\" We do know these devices\n        are used to secure private keys for blockchain transactions, but we\n        figured we''d extend their capabilities.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>But I don''t want to turn my hardware wallet into a reader!</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>Understandable. If you change your mind you can always come back on\n        this website.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>Ok, how does it work?</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>Simple: for each book we created an app that runs on BOLOS (the\n        Ledger device operating system) which renders the text and manages\n        page turning. We designed a reading experience optimized for the\n        constraints of the device. You choose a book from the website, plug\n        your device in, install the app, and you can start reading.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>My device asks to allow an unknown source. Should I?</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>Read the screen, then decide. That prompt is your device telling you\n        the truth: this app is not in Ledger''s catalogue and was never\n        submitted to it, so nobody has checked it but us. You can read the\n        code at github.com/s0lness/ledger-ereader, or ask your favourite\n        agent to read it for you.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>Can this touch my coins?</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>The reader makes no keys, asks for no derivation path, never sees\n        your recovery phrase and has no network. It draws text on a screen.</p>\n        <p>Installing any app is a write to the device, which is why it asks\n        for your PIN: that authorises the installation, it does not hand\n        anything over. Your accounts and your phrase are untouched by it,\n        and removing the app leaves nothing behind.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>Do you have the rights to the books published?</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>We only edit public domain books.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>Who is behind this? Are you affiliated with Ledger?</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>Sylve Chevet, a former Ledger employee, figured it''d be fun. It''s\n        only him working on this project. Not affiliated with Ledger.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary><h3>I''d like to request a book or ask a question</h3></summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-a\">\n        <p>Contact Sylve through his website: sylve.org</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n  </section>\n\n</main>\n\n<footer class=\"bar bar-foot\">\n  <div class=\"sheet bar-in\">\n    <span>Enclave Press · Paris</span>\n  </div>\n</footer>\n\n<script src=\"press.js?v=11\"></script>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/v4513226cdae34746b4dedf0b4dfa099e1781791509496\" integrity=\"sha512-ZE9pZaUXND66v380QUtch/5sE9tPFh2zg45pR2PB0CVkCtOREv2AJKkSidISWkysEuQ0EH8faUU5du78bx87UQ==\" data-cf-beacon=\"{&quot;version&quot;:&quot;2024.11.0&quot;,&quot;token&quot;:&quot;c4bd9f827ea2476aa787bf18cd66ef99&quot;,&quot;r&quot;:1}\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n\n\n<div data-markup-ui=\"\"></div><a id=\"bottomBar\" style=\"position: fixed; bottom: -40px; left: 0px; z-index: 9999; transform: translateX(-50%); background-color: transparent; border-radius: 5px 5px 0px 0px; opacity: 0.3; padding: 5px; transition: 0.3s; cursor: pointer; max-height: 100px; max-width: 45px;\"><img src=\"chrome-extension://kobncfkmjelbefaoohoblamnbackjggk/icon/icon_32.png\" style=\"width: 32px; height: 32px;\"></a></body>","visible":["main.sheet > section.hero:nth-of-type(1)","main.sheet > section.hero:nth-of-type(1) > div.hero-txt:nth-of-type(1) > h1 \"Read on your Ledger\"","div#questions > h2 \"Questions\"","main.sheet > section.faq:nth-of-type(2)"]}},"collection|1":{"type":"n","viewport":{"w":2560,"h":1305},"theme":"dark","ts":"2026-08-07T09:01:04.618Z","attached":[],"state":{"html":"<body>\n\n<a class=\"skip\" href=\"#shelf\">Skip to the books</a>\n\n<header class=\"bar\">\n  <div class=\"sheet bar-in\">\n    <a class=\"house\" href=\"index.html\">\n      <span class=\"mark\" data-mark=\"\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"45\" height=\"42\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 14\" shape-rendering=\"crispEdges\" fill=\"#000\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"0\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"6\" y=\"0\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"10\" y=\"0\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"1\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"6\" y=\"1\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"10\" y=\"1\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"2\" width=\"15\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"3\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"3\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"4\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"8\" y=\"4\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"4\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"5\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"8\" y=\"5\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"11\" y=\"5\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"5\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"6\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"3\" y=\"6\" width=\"3\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"8\" y=\"6\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"6\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"7\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"3\" y=\"7\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"8\" y=\"7\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"7\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"8\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"3\" y=\"8\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"8\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"9\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"3\" y=\"9\" width=\"4\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"8\" y=\"9\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"9\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"10\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"14\" y=\"10\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"0\" y=\"11\" width=\"15\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"12\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"6\" y=\"12\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"2\" y=\"13\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"6\" y=\"13\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"10\" y=\"13\" width=\"2\" height=\"1\"></rect></svg></span>\n      <span class=\"house-name\"><b>ENCLAVE</b><b>PRESS</b></span>\n    </a>\n    <nav class=\"bar-nav\">\n      <a href=\"collection.html\" aria-current=\"page\">Books</a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/s0lness/ledger-ereader\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Code</a>\n    </nav>\n  </div>\n</header>\n\n<main class=\"sheet\">\n\n  <!-- Only the books. The heading stays in the document for a reader that\n       needs one, and off the page for one that does not: the covers say what\n       this is faster than a word can. -->\n  <h1 class=\"off-screen\">Books</h1>\n\n  <div class=\"shelf\" id=\"shelf\" data-shelf=\"\">\n    <a class=\"rel\" href=\"bitcoin.html\">\n      <span class=\"plate-box\"><img class=\"plate\" src=\"assets/bitcoin-plate.png\" alt=\"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System, its cover as the device draws it\"></span>\n      <span class=\"rel-line\">\n        <span class=\"rel-title\">Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System</span>\n        \n        <span class=\"rel-by\">Satoshi Nakamoto</span>\n      </span>\n    </a>\n    <a class=\"rel\" href=\"gatsby.html\">\n      <span class=\"plate-box\"><img class=\"plate\" src=\"assets/gatsby-plate.png\" alt=\"The Great Gatsby, its cover as the device draws it\"></span>\n      <span class=\"rel-line\">\n        <span class=\"rel-title\">The Great Gatsby</span>\n        \n        <span class=\"rel-by\">F. Scott Fitzgerald</span>\n      </span>\n    </a></div>\n\n</main>\n\n<footer class=\"bar bar-foot\">\n  <div class=\"sheet bar-in\">\n    <span>Enclave Press · Paris</span>\n  </div>\n</footer>\n\n<script>\n/* `ready` is the one thing on this shelf that can be wrong, so it is kept\n   equal to whether the book''s own page has an `apdu` to offer. A title that\n   says Free here and Not ready yet one click later is worse than either. */\nwindow.SHELF = [\n  /* Back on, with the cause of the two wipes found and compiled in. The\n     details are on bitcoin.html, beside the `apdu` line it carries again. */\n  { href: ''bitcoin.html'', title: ''Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System'',\n    author: ''Satoshi Nakamoto'', pages: 90, ready: true, plate: ''assets/bitcoin-plate.png'' },\n  { href: ''gatsby.html'', title: ''The Great Gatsby'', author: ''F. Scott Fitzgerald'',\n    pages: 938, ready: true, plate: ''assets/gatsby-plate.png'' },\n];\n</script>\n<script src=\"press.js?v=11\"></script>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/v4513226cdae34746b4dedf0b4dfa099e1781791509496\" integrity=\"sha512-ZE9pZaUXND66v380QUtch/5sE9tPFh2zg45pR2PB0CVkCtOREv2AJKkSidISWkysEuQ0EH8faUU5du78bx87UQ==\" data-cf-beacon=\"{&quot;version&quot;:&quot;2024.11.0&quot;,&quot;token&quot;:&quot;c4bd9f827ea2476aa787bf18cd66ef99&quot;,&quot;r&quot;:1}\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n\n\n<div data-markup-ui=\"\"></div><a id=\"bottomBar\" style=\"position: fixed; bottom: -40px; left: 0px; z-index: 9999; transform: translateX(-50%); background-color: transparent; border-radius: 5px 5px 0px 0px; opacity: 0.3; padding: 5px; transition: 0.3s; cursor: pointer; max-height: 100px; max-width: 45px;\"><img src=\"chrome-extension://kobncfkmjelbefaoohoblamnbackjggk/icon/icon_32.png\" style=\"width: 32px; height: 32px;\"></a></body>","visible":["main.sheet > h1.off-screen \"Books\""]},"note":"i''d like to have a \"request a book\" button here that would send a request \"somewhere\" that i could read"},"gatsby|1":{"type":"n","viewport":{"w":2560,"h":1305},"theme":"dark","ts":"2026-08-07T09:02:08.654Z","attached":[],"state":{"html":"<div class=\"screen\" data-screen=\"\"><div class=\"board\"><img class=\"plate\" src=\"assets/gatsby-plate.png\" alt=\"The Great Gatsby, its cover as the device draws it\"></div></div>","visible":["div.rail:nth-of-type(1) > div.rail-stick > div.device > div.screen","div#step > div.step","div#step > div.step > h1.tall \"The Great Gatsby\""]},"note":"would love to have the emulator running with the book here"},"gatsby|2":{"type":"f","viewport":{"w":2560,"h":1305},"theme":"dark","ts":"2026-08-07T09:02:22.911Z","attached":[],"state":{"html":"<main class=\"sheet\">\n  <div class=\"spread\">\n    <div class=\"rail\">\n      <div class=\"rail-stick\">\n        <div class=\"device\" data-device=\"\"><div class=\"screen\" data-screen=\"\"><div class=\"board\"><img class=\"plate\" src=\"assets/gatsby-plate.png\" alt=\"The Great Gatsby, its cover as the device draws it\"></div></div></div>\n        <p class=\"rail-cap\" data-railcap=\"\"></p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"column\" id=\"step\">\n      <div class=\"step\" data-step=\"\">\n    <h1 class=\"tall\">The Great Gatsby</h1>\n    <p class=\"byline\">F. Scott Fitzgerald</p>\n    <div class=\"blurb\"><p>A man buys a house across the water from a green light and gives\n    parties for five years in the hope that one person walks into one of them.\n    Fitzgerald published it in 1925, sold badly, died believing he had failed,\n    and left behind the shortest great American novel.</p>\n    <p>It entered the public domain in 2021. Enclave Press did not buy it,\n    cannot own it, and does not gate it.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"acts\">\n      <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"PRESS.go(''dlstart'')\">Download book</button>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</main>","visible":["div.rail:nth-of-type(1) > div.rail-stick > div.device > div.screen","div#step > div.step","div#step > div.step > h1.tall \"The Great Gatsby\""]},"note":"would need a \"back\" button here to go back to all books; same for all books"}},"textEdits":[],"notes":[],"pins":[],"svg":{"bitcoin":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1521\" height=\"951\" viewBox=\"0 0 1521 951\"></svg>"}}','applied','5f5156de3f63221a657a6aebbe8a0efdbbe1dfd1','2026-08-07 13:48:40');
