rn cryptocurrencies.\n    Laying out an elegant and simple design for Internet-native money, it also\n    paved the way for a more global architecture supporting Bitcoin:\n    blockchain.</p>\n    <p>This edition is adapted for the Ledger Flex. Diagrams have been redrawn\n    to fit the screen sizes and tweaked for readability. Equations and code\n    have been reformatted for the same reason.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"acts\">\n      <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"PRESS.go(''dlstart'')\">Download book</button>\n      <span class=\"tally\" data-count=\"bitcoin\">1 download</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>","visible":["main.sheet > div.spread > div.bookhead:nth-of-type(1) > h1.tall \"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash \"","div.rail:nth-of-type(2) > div.rail-stick > div.device > div.screen","div#step > div.step"]},"note":"remove the number of downloads everywhere"},"bitcoin|3":{"type":"n","viewport":{"w":2560,"h":1305},"theme":"dark","ts":"2026-08-10T08:15:08.891Z","attached":[],"state":{"html":"<div class=\"screen\" data-screen=\"\"><div class=\"board\"><span class=\"rail-live\">\n      <iframe class=\"live\" src=\"try/index.html?book=bitcoin&amp;bare\" loading=\"lazy\" scrolling=\"no\" title=\"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System, running: tap the screen to turn a page\"></iframe>\n      <span class=\"sheen\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n    </span></div></div>","visible":["main.sheet > div.spread > div.bookhead:nth-of-type(1) > h1.tall \"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash \"","div.rail:nth-of-type(2) > div.rail-stick > div.device > div.screen","div#step > div.step"]},"note":"during the installation flow i want all instructions to be seen on this \"frame\" only. I want the text description on the right hand side to never change."},"index|1":{"type":"f","viewport":{"w":2560,"h":1305},"theme":"dark","ts":"2026-08-10T08:31:09.905Z","attached":[],"state":{"html":"<section class=\"hero\">\n\n    <div class=\"hero-txt\">\n      <h1>Read on your Ledger</h1>\n      <p class=\"hero-lede\">Enclave Press edits books to read on Ledger Devices. Leveraging the\n      portability and e-ink screens of the devices, you can now transform\n      your hardware wallet into a reader.</p>\n      <div class=\"acts\">\n        <a class=\"btn\" href=\"collection.html\">See the books</a>\n        <!-- The reader itself, in the page. `sim/` runs the device''s own\n             pagination and its own atlases, so this is not a mock-up of the\n             thing: it is the thing, minus the panel. -->\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- The device is drawn here, not photographed: an oblique extrusion,\n         shaded and quantised by the same Bayer matrix the covers are cut\n         with, so the object is made of the covers'' own material. The panel\n         stays frontal and the cover sits in its recess at 1x. -->\n    <div class=\"hero-obj\">\n      <div class=\"flex\">\n        <img class=\"flex-shell\" src=\"assets/flex-shell.png\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"584\" height=\"704\">\n        <!-- The whitepaper, because it is the newest title and the one the\n             shelf leads with. Swapping this line and its alt text is the whole\n             of changing which book the front page shows. -->\n        <!-- THE READER, RUNNING. Not a picture of one: this is `sim/`, the\n             same pagination and the same atlases the device carries, in the\n             recess the drawn Flex leaves for a screen. A visitor taps the\n             glass and the page turns, which is the only honest way to show\n             what the thing is. `?bare` strips the bench''s own frame so the\n             only device on the page is the one drawn around it. -->\n        <span class=\"plate-box flex-plate\">\n          <iframe class=\"plate live\" src=\"try/index.html?book=bitcoin&amp;bare\" title=\"The reader, running: tap the screen to turn a page\" loading=\"lazy\" scrolling=\"no\"></iframe>\n          <!-- The glass. A layer over the panel, not a change to it: the\n               reader''s pixels are the device''s pixels and nothing here is\n               allowed to alter one. It takes no clicks, so a tap goes\n               through to the page underneath. -->\n          <span class=\"glass\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n          <!-- The sheen: the one thing on the page that moves, and the only\n               reason a visitor learns the drawing is live without touching\n               it first. -->\n          <span class=\"sheen\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        </span>\n      </div>\n      <!-- Nothing under the device and nothing written on it. There was a\n           caption (\"Tap the screen. It is the reader, running.\") and then a\n           label in the bezel (\"Tap to read\"), and the owner cut both on\n           2026-08-07. The sheen is what says the drawing is alive; a sentence\n           explaining a self-sufficient visual is the one thing this house\n           does not do. -->\n    </div>\n\n  </section>","visible":["main.sheet > section.hero:nth-of-type(1)","main.sheet > section.hero:nth-of-type(1) > div.hero-txt:nth-of-type(1) > h1 \"Read on your Ledger\"","div#questions > h2 \"Questions\"","main.sheet > section.faq:nth-of-type(2)"]}},"index|2":{"type":"f","viewport":{"w":2560,"h":1305},"theme":"dark","ts":"2026-08-10T08:31:10.152Z","attached":[],"state":{"html":"<section class=\"hero\">\n\n    <div class=\"hero-txt\">\n      <h1>Read on your Ledger</h1>\n      <p class=\"hero-lede\">Enclave Press edits books to read on Ledger Devices. Leveraging the\n      portability and e-ink screens of the devices, you can now transform\n      your hardware wallet into a reader.</p>\n      <div class=\"acts\">\n        <a class=\"btn\" href=\"collection.html\">See the books</a>\n        <!-- The reader itself, in the page. `sim/` runs the device''s own\n             pagination and its own atlases, so this is not a mock-up of the\n             thing: it is the thing, minus the panel. -->\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- The device is drawn here, not photographed: an oblique extrusion,\n         shaded and quantised by the same Bayer matrix the covers are cut\n         with, so the object is made of the covers'' own material. The panel\n         stays frontal and the cover sits in its recess at 1x. -->\n    <div class=\"hero-obj\">\n      <div class=\"flex\">\n        <img class=\"flex-shell\" src=\"assets/flex-shell.png\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"584\" height=\"704\">\n        <!-- The whitepaper, because it is the newest title and the one the\n             shelf leads with. Swapping this line and its alt text is the whole\n             of changing which book the front page shows. -->\n        <!-- THE READER, RUNNING. Not a picture of one: this is `sim/`, the\n             same pagination and the same atlases the device carries, in the\n             recess the drawn Flex leaves for a screen. A visitor taps the\n             glass and the page turns, which is the only honest way to show\n             what the thing is. `?bare` strips the bench''s own frame so the\n             only device on the page is the one drawn around it. -->\n        <span class=\"plate-box flex-plate\">\n          <iframe class=\"plate live\" src=\"try/index.html?book=bitcoin&amp;bare\" title=\"The reader, running: tap the screen to turn a page\" loading=\"lazy\" scrolling=\"no\"></iframe>\n          <!-- The glass. A layer over the panel, not a change to it: the\n               reader''s pixels are the device''s pixels and nothing here is\n               allowed to alter one. It takes no clicks, so a tap goes\n               through to the page underneath. -->\n          <span class=\"glass\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n          <!-- The sheen: the one thing on the page that moves, and the only\n               reason a visitor learns the drawing is live without touching\n               it first. -->\n          <span class=\"sheen\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        </span>\n      </div>\n      <!-- Nothing under the device and nothing written on it. There was a\n           caption (\"Tap the screen. It is the reader, running.\") and then a\n           label in the bezel (\"Tap to read\"), and the owner cut both on\n           2026-08-07. The sheen is what says the drawing is alive; a sentence\n           explaining a self-sufficient visual is the one thing this house\n           does not do. -->\n    </div>\n\n  </section>","visible":["main.sheet > section.hero:nth-of-type(1)","main.sheet > section.hero:nth-of-type(1) > div.hero-txt:nth-of-type(1) > h1 \"Read on your Ledger\"","div#questions > h2 \"Questions\"","main.sheet > section.faq:nth-of-type(2)"]},"note":"there''s sort of a useless \"line\" here on device emulator, remove it."}},"textEdits":[],"notes":[],"pins":[],"svg":{"index":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2545\" height=\"1749\" viewBox=\"0 0 2545 1749\"><path d=\"M1473.4,784L1471.7,784L1471.7,778L1473.4,778ZM1476.1,781L1475.7,782.5L1474.5,783.7L1473,784.1L1471.5,783.7L1470.3,782.5L1469.9,781L1470.3,779.5L1471.5,778.3L1473,777.9L1474.5,778.3L1475.7,779.5ZM1473.5,783.6L1472,784.3L1469.6,778.8L1471.1,778.1ZM1475.1,781L1474.7,782.5L1473.5,783.7L1472,784.1L1470.5,783.7L1469.3,782.5L1468.9,781L1469.3,779.5L1470.5,778.3L1472,777.9L1473.5,778.3L1474.7,779.5ZM1472.8,783.9L1471.3,784.7L1468.5,779.4L1470,778.6ZM1474.2,781.4L1473.8,782.9L1472.6,784.1L1471.1,784.5L1469.5,784.1L1468.4,782.9L1468,781.4L1468.4,779.8L1469.5,778.7L1471.1,778.3L1472.6,778.7L1473.8,779.8ZM1472.3,784L1471,785L1467.3,780.3L1468.7,779.3ZM1473.3,781.9L1472.9,783.4L1471.8,784.5L1470.2,784.9L1468.7,784.5L1467.5,783.4L1467.1,781.9L1467.5,780.3L1468.7,779.2L1470.2,778.8L1471.8,779.2L1472.9,780.3ZM1472.1,783.8L1471.1,785.2L1466.2,781.9L1467.2,780.5ZM1472.5,782.4L1472.1,784L1471,785.1L1469.4,785.5L1467.9,785.1L1466.8,784L1466.3,782.4L1466.8,780.9L1467.9,779.8L1469.4,779.4L1471,779.8L1472.1,780.9ZM1471.5,784.7L1470.